  <p>Wholesale gym wear in Australia is a competitive market. Buyers need products that look premium, fit well, ship reliably, and do not trap cash in slow-moving inventory. The key is choosing the right sourcing model before you order.</p>

  <h2>Three Sourcing Models for Australian Gym Wear Buyers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Ready-stock wholesale:</strong> fastest route for new stores, gyms, and small online sellers.</li>
    <li><strong>Private label stock styles:</strong> adds logo, label, and packaging while keeping MOQ manageable.</li>
    <li><strong>Custom manufacturing:</strong> best for established brands that need exclusive design and repeat orders.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What Products Sell Well for Australian Gym Wear</h2>
  <p>Australian customers often respond well to versatile activewear that can move between training, pilates, errands, and casual wear. This makes neutral color yoga sets, squat-proof leggings, supportive sports bras, oversized tees, bike shorts, and lightweight layers strong starting points.</p>

  <h2>How to Reduce Inventory Risk</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Start with fewer colors and stronger size curves.</li>
    <li>Use ready-stock or low-MOQ private label styles for first testing.</li>
    <li>Order samples in the exact colors and fabrics you plan to sell.</li>
    <li>Review customer feedback before moving into custom OEM.</li>
    <li>Reserve best-selling fabric and color options for repeat production.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Key Supplier Questions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>What is the MOQ per style, color, and size?</li>
    <li>Can you support logo application and branded packaging?</li>
    <li>What are the sample and bulk lead times?</li>
    <li>Can you provide videos of fabric stretch, opacity, and stitching?</li>
    <li>Can you prepare shipping documents for Australia?</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Fitclo's Recommendation</h2>
  <p>For most Australian wholesale gym wear buyers, the safest route is to start with private label stock styles and a focused SKU plan. Once a style proves demand, you can upgrade into custom color, custom fabric, or full OEM development.</p>
